 ## Overview
-Probabilistic Directed Distance Fields (PDDFs) are a variant of Directed Distance Fields (DDFs) designed to differentiably model the inherent discontinuities in the underlying field, specifically surface and occlusion discontinuities [S1, S2]. While standard DDFs output a single scalar depth value, PDDFs modify the formulation so that the network outputs probability distributions over rays rather than a single value, allowing a $C^1$ continuous neural network to represent the discontinuous field of a DDF [S1]. This enables efficient differentiable rendering and geometry extraction via network derivatives [S1, S2].
